    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">We are pleased to invite you to our next webinar: <strong>Strengthening the Electoral Profession: How to Improve Knowledge Sharing</strong>, taking place on <strong>Thursday, 4 June 2026 at 14:00&ndash;15:15 UTC (15:00&ndash;16:15 BST)</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Electoral bodies build extraordinary institutional knowledge. Through every cycle they run, they develop systems, train staff, navigate new challenges, and find better ways to administer elections. Yet much of that knowledge stays locked within institutions &mdash; or disappears when staff move on.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Across the electoral industry, the same challenges are being navigated in parallel, the same ground is being covered independently, and the connections that would make every institution stronger remain unmade. The information that matters &mdash; legislative developments, peer institution experience, sector research, regulatory updates &mdash; is scattered across newsletters, alerts, and informal networks built up over years.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 24px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">ICPS brings together leading voices across electoral management to ask: what would it mean for the electoral sector to share knowledge more effectively? And what does a practical improvement actually look like?</p>

